Hey Reem,

Imo TMP is almost always the better option compared to using a linear model in the summarization step. Check out the example below (it uses TMT but the idea is the same). Log Sum really just follows the highest feature. Linear is better but is very effected by noisy features (outliers/missing values/ect). TMP is more robust to these issues, which makes it less impacted by noisy features.

I suppose linear might be better in cases where you either expect your data to not be too noisy, or in cases where you really want to capture the noise. I would recommend checking out a couple profile plots using both methods to see the impact!

Best,
Devon

